Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
publication_number: identifies each patent publication.  
country_code: filter to U S patents (value = 'US').  
kind_code: filter to granted patents of type B2.  
grant_date: numeric yyyymmdd; keep those between 20080101 and 20181231.  
claims_localized: VARIANT array that stores the claim texts (plain‑text version).  
claims_localized_html: VARIANT array that stores an HTML version of the same claims (can be used if the plain text is missing).  

Typical conditions that may be useful  
country_code = 'US'  
kind_code = 'B2'  
grant_date BETWEEN 20080101 AND 20181231  
NOT (LOWER(claim_text) ILIKE '%claim%')  -- to detect a claim that does not contain the word “claim”  
All claims of a patent fail the test – i.e. no claim within the patent contains the string “claim”.  

Below are 10 exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (each capped with LIMIT 20) that move step‑by‑step from simple inspection to the final answer.  
```sql
-- 1. Description: Quick look at a handful of rows in the PUBLICATIONS table.
SELECT 
  "publication_number",
  "country_code",
  "kind_code",
  "grant_date",
  "claims_localized"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Distinct kind codes used for US publications.
SELECT DISTINCT "kind_code"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE "country_code" = 'US'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Distinct (country, kind_code, application_kind) triples to confirm that ‘B2’ corresponds to granted utility patents.
SELECT DISTINCT 
  "country_code",
  "kind_code",
  "application_kind"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE "country_code" = 'US'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Sample of US B2 patents granted 2008‑2018 to verify date filtering.
SELECT 
  "publication_number",
  "grant_date",
  "title_localized"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE "country_code" = 'US'
  AND "kind_code" = 'B2'
  AND "grant_date" BETWEEN 20080101 AND 20181231
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Peek inside the structure of the variant column “claims_localized”.
SELECT 
  "publication_number",
  f.value AS "claim_variant"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."claims_localized") f
WHERE p."country_code" = 'US'
  AND p."kind_code" = 'B2'
  AND p."grant_date" BETWEEN 20080101 AND 20181231
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Extract the actual claim text (assuming each element has a “text” field).
SELECT 
  p."publication_number",
  f.value:"language"::STRING  AS "lang",
  f.value:"text"::STRING      AS "claim_text"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."claims_localized") f
WHERE p."country_code" = 'US'
  AND p."kind_code" = 'B2'
  AND p."grant_date" BETWEEN 20080101 AND 20181231
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Find individual claims (not patents yet) whose text does NOT contain the word “claim”.
SELECT 
  p."publication_number",
  f.value:"text"::STRING AS "claim_text_without_word"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."claims_localized") f
WHERE p."country_code" = 'US'
  AND p."kind_code" = 'B2'
  AND p."grant_date" BETWEEN 20080101 AND 20181231
  AND LOWER(f.value:"text"::STRING) NOT ILIKE '%claim%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Retrieve every B2 patent that has at least one claim lacking the word “claim”.
SELECT DISTINCT
  p."publication_number"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."claims_localized") f
WHERE p."country_code" = 'US'
  AND p."kind_code" = 'B2'
  AND p."grant_date" BETWEEN 20080101 AND 20181231
  AND LOWER(f.value:"text"::STRING) NOT ILIKE '%claim%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Ensure no claim in the patent contains the word “claim”
--    by counting total claims vs. those containing the word.
SELECT 
  p."publication_number"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p
WHERE p."country_code" = 'US'
  AND p."kind_code" = 'B2'
  AND p."grant_date" BETWEEN 20080101 AND 20181231
  AND NOT EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."claims_localized") f
        WHERE LOWER(f.value:"text"::STRING) ILIKE '%claim%'
      )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--10. Description: Final tally – number of US B2 patents (2008‑2018) whose claims never use the word “claim”.
SELECT 
  COUNT(*) AS "patent_count_no_word_claim"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p
WHERE p."country_code" = 'US'
  AND p."kind_code" = 'B2'
  AND p."grant_date" BETWEEN 20080101 AND 20181231
  AND NOT EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."claims_localized") f
        WHERE LOWER(f.value:"text"::STRING) ILIKE '%claim%'
      )
LIMIT 20;
```
